Revision history for App-Clod

0.002 (not yet released)
    - Fail a fix or an answer to a review that made no commit because
      claude refused some of its calls, and name each refused call in the
      error.  Such a run finished as no change before, with a reply that
      said the change was made.
    - With run_as, the account that claude runs as brings its own Claude
      token.  sudo logged the token of the worker, which went through
      --preserve-env, with its value.
    - Allow each Bash permission rule for the command that rtk makes of it,
      so that an unattended run is not refused every git and prove.
    - Make a new repository when an authorized user asks for one, if
      create_repos names the organizations where the bot may, then work in it
      like any other spoke and open an issue for its first release.
    - File a follow-up issue in a spoke when an authorized user asks for one,
      assigned to them, with follow_up_max as the cap of one request.

0.001 2026-10-28 TEODESIAN
    - Initial Release
